eq v (up to scaling) produces the same distribution over observable outputs across all prompts and steering strengths. Definition 2 (Observational Equivalence). Two steering vectors v v and v ′ v^{\prime} are observationally equivalent in regime ℛ \mathcal{R} if they produce identical distributions over all quantities observable in ℛ \mathcal{R} . For Regime 2 (white-box single-layer access): v ∼ ℛ v ′ ⇔ F ℓ → L ( h ℓ ( x ) + α v ) \displaystyle v\sim_{\mathcal{R}}v^{\prime}\iff F_{\ell	o L}(h_{\ell}(x)+\alpha v) (1) = F ℓ → L ​ ( h ℓ ​ ( x ) + α ​ v ′ ) ​ ∀ x , α . \displaystyle=F_{\ell	o L}(h_{\ell}(x)+\alpha v^{\prime})\; orall x,\alpha. 4.2 Symmetries and Gauge Freedom Scaling ambiguity. For any c ≠ 0 c
